@node Nuevo40 "AmiMSX Emulator."

@{fg highlight}    New in 4.x:
@{fg text}    -----------

    AmiMSX 4.x is a community update of AmiMSX, made with the permission
of Juan Antonio Gómez Gálvez.  It is built from his v3.1 source, with
parts of his later v3.2/v3.5 source.  Accuracy comes first.

    Please report any game that misbehaves as an issue on GitHub, with the game, the AmiMSX settings and your machine:
https://github.com/z00p/AmiMSX/issues

    - Z80:  POP/RET through ROM, RLD/RRD on ROM, NEG/CPL flags, M1 wait
      states, LD A,R from emulated time.

    - VDP:  sprite collisions, the 5th sprite flag, sprite mode 2 bands,
      mid-frame splits, transparent copies, LMMC.

    - MSX2+:  the machine is back, with the V9958 fine scroll (R#27) and
      left mask (R#25).  (See @{"MSX2 Display Emulation" link Dibuixos}.)

    - Sound:  MSX-Music (FM) on Amiga channel 3, PSG volume in 3 dB
      steps.  (See @{"MSX2 Sound Emulation" link Soroll}.)

    - Display:  double-buffered sprites, Smooth display for fast CPUs,
      an edge mask of 8 or 16 dots for games that scroll sideways.

    - Options:  Use Japanese ID (60 Hz), Mask screen edges (Off, 8 or
      16 dots), Audio filter, Smooth display.  (See @{"Options Menu" link MenuOpt}.)

    - Cartridges:  mapper from a ROM database, 8Kb, 48/64Kb and 4Mb
      ROMs, flash Konami SCC cartridges with saves, per-game settings.
      (See @{"Cartridges Menu" link MenuCar}.)

    - Disks:  drive B with its own disk image, disk swap with Left Amiga.
      (See @{"MSX Virtual Drive Menu" link MenuMVD}.)

    - Two @{"presets" link Presets}: one for a 68030, one for PiStorm and
      other fast CPUs.

    The full list is in Docs/CHANGES_4.x.txt.


@{fg highlight}    Credits for 4.x:
@{fg text}    ----------------

    AmiMSX:    Juan Antonio Gómez Gálvez, GUS Entertainment / RED Soft
    Graphics:  Multivac
    Thanks:    Zener and Sandman

@endnode


@node Presets "AmiMSX Emulator."

@{fg highlight}    Presets:
@{fg text}    --------

    Start AmiMSX from one of the two preset icons.  Each one has its own
settings file, and Save Prefs writes to the preset you started.

@{fg highlight}    <*> AmiMSX 030:
@{fg text}    ---------------

    The low-spec target:  an A1200 or similar with a 68030 at 50Mhz and
Fast memory.  PSG, PAL, sprites every frame.

@{fg highlight}    <*> AmiMSX PiStorm:
@{fg text}    -------------------

    PiStorm (Emu68), BigMig and other fast CPUs.  PSG+FM, Frequence
[From VDP] (60 Hz games in NTSC, at full speed), Use Japanese ID (60 Hz),
Audio filter and Smooth display.

@{fg highlight}    <*> ToolType PREFS=<file>:
@{fg text}    --------------------------

    Chooses the settings file.  A relative name is taken from the icon's
drawer.  Without it, AmiMSX uses S:MSX2emulator.prefs.

@endnode


@node Autor "AmiMSX Emulator."

@{fg highlight}    Note from author:
@{fg text}    -----------------

    Hola Amigos!!!!

    A new update of AmiMSX, new features:

    - MSX2 Overscan support. (256x224 pixels)  (Sex Bomb Bunny)
    - Screen 2 and 4 ONE tile bank support.  (Ark-A-Noah)
    - Screen 8 Sprites are now emulated with your real colours.
    - Syncronized CPU emulation. (Real / Fast / Turbo modes)
    - 100% Compatible with all Motorola Procesors. (020/030/040/060)
    - Full support of Line Interrupts.


    There are two games included with AmiMSX to test these two features:

    Sex Bomb Bunny:  A sexy game in Screen 8 with overscan support.

    Ark-A-Noah:  A game in Screen 4 with overscan support and uses
ONE bank tiles instead of 4.

    These two games ONLY works 100% with AmiMSX, I not found any other
MSX emulator capable of emulate them correctly!!!

    These games are © Matra Corporation 'www.matranet.net' A new group
making great games for MSX.  Take a look to your web!!!!

    Greetings!

    Juan

@endnode


@node Introduccio "AmiMSX Emulator."

@{fg highlight}    Introduction:
@{fg text}    -------------

    This program emulates a 8-bit MSX2 computer.

    Quality of emulation depends on the Amiga system that is used.

    This program does not multitask and freezes the Operating System to
obtain a good quality emulation, programming directly the Amiga's custom
chips.


@{fg highlight}    DISCLAIMER:
@{fg text}    -----------
    THE AUTHOR DOESN'T GUARANTEE THAT THIS PROGRAM EMULATES A FULL MSX2,
AND ACCEPTS NO RESPONSIBILITY FOR LOSS OF DATA DERIVED FROM THE USE OF
THIS SOFTWARE...

@endnode


@node Requeriments "AmiMSX Emulator."

@{fg highlight}    <*>  Minimal Requirements:
@{fg text}    --------------------------

    - AMIGA computer with AGA chipset  (On ECS AmiMSX warns first.)
    - MC68030+
    - AmigaOS 3.0+
    - DEVS:mfm.device           (For DiskDrives emulation)
    - DEVS:statram.device       (For RAMSX: drive emulation)
    - LIBS:stc020.library v3.0+
    - LIBS:asl.library
    - 3MB of memory (1Mb Chip)
    - PAL, NTSC or compatible monitor.

@{fg highlight}    <*>  Recommended:
@{fg text}    -----------------

    - MC68030 at 50Mz with 32-bit Fast memory  (the "AmiMSX 030" preset)

    - PiStorm (Emu68), BigMig or another fast CPU for MSX-Music (FM),
      60 Hz games at full speed and Smooth display  (the "AmiMSX PiStorm"
      preset)

    A stock 68020 A1200 runs AmiMSX, but slowly.  (See @{"Presets" link Presets}.)

@endnode


